IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`

-- ccc20-tests-fixtures.l4 -- named values the ccc20 test files share (offences and classes of offence). No rule, no assertion.
-- Every name begins with the section label it serves, like every other top-level name of this part.

`s 493.01 fixture class indictable`   MEANS `an indictable offence`
`s 493.01 fixture class hybrid`       MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
`s 493.01 fixture class summary`      MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- the offence charged, as s 493.01 describes it (class, and whether the prosecutor has elected summary conviction)
`s 493.01 fixture indictable`         MEANS `s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an indictable offence`, FALSE
`s 493.01 fixture hybrid`             MEANS `s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, FALSE
`s 493.01 fixture hybrid elected`     MEANS `s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, TRUE
`s 493.01 fixture summary`            MEANS `s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence punishable on summary conviction`, FALSE
